---
// The account-deletion page, which Google Play requires as a *separate* URL
// from the privacy policy.
//
// The Data Safety form's "Delete data URL" has three stated requirements, and
// the privacy page met only the first: name the app or developer, prominently
// feature the steps, and specify what is deleted or kept with any retention
// period. A one-line "email us" satisfies none of the last two.
//
// **The honest part is the second table.** Deactivating a Matrix account does
// not unsend anything: a message is an event copied to every server
// participating in the room, and those copies are not ours to delete. A
// template would promise erasure here, and the promise would be false in a
// document a regulator may read.
//
// The head and styles are lifted from privacy.astro deliberately, so the two
// compliance pages cannot drift apart visually.
import '../styles/tokens.css';
import ShareMeta from '../components/ShareMeta.astro';

const title = 'Delete your account — supermessage';
const description =
  'How to ask for your supermessage account and its data to be deleted, and exactly what is removed.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <ShareMeta title={title} description={description} />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,400;12..96,600;12..96,800&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        --display: 'Bricolage Grotesque', 'Trebuchet MS', sans-serif;
        --body: 'IBM Plex Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--color-surface-sunken);
        color: var(--color-content);
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-size: 17px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }

      main {
        max-width: 68ch;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 48px 24px 96px;
      }

      a { color: var(--color-accent); }

      h1 {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 44px);
        line-height: 1.1;
        margin: 0 0 8px;
      }

      h2 {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-size: 22px;
        margin: 40px 0 8px;
      }

      .updated { color: var(--color-content-muted); margin: 0 0 40px; }

      /* The one claim a reader is most likely to be surprised by, so it is
         the one thing on the page given a surface of its own. */
      .callout {
        background: var(--color-surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        border-left: 3px solid var(--color-signal);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 16px 20px;
        margin: 24px 0;
      }

      table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 16px 0; }
      th, td {
        text-align: left;
        padding: 10px 12px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        vertical-align: top;
      }
      th { font-weight: 600; }
      td:first-child { white-space: nowrap; }

      footer {
        margin-top: 56px;
        padding-top: 24px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        color: var(--color-content-muted);
        font-size: 15px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Delete your account</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated 15 September 2026</p>

      <p>
        This page is for <strong>supermessage</strong>, published by
        <strong>Super Jackfruit Labs (OPC) Private Limited</strong>. It explains how to have
        your account deleted and exactly what that does and does not remove.
      </p>

      <h2>How to request deletion</h2>

      <ol>
        <li>
          Email <a href="mailto:privacy@superjackfruit.com">privacy@superjackfruit.com</a> from
          an address we can associate with you, with the subject
          <strong>Delete my account</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Include your <strong>Matrix user ID</strong> — it looks like
          <code>@you:id.agentpod.dev</code> and is shown in the app under Account.
        </li>
        <li>
          We reply to confirm it is really you before doing anything, because an
          unverified request is a way to delete somebody else's account.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p>
        We action confirmed requests within <strong>30 days</strong>, and usually much sooner.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>This applies to accounts on <code>id.agentpod.dev</code>, the homeserver we
        operate.</strong> If you signed in with an account on a different Matrix homeserver, we
        never held your data and cannot delete it — ask whoever runs that server.
      </div>

      <h2>What is deleted</h2>

      <table>
        <tr><th>Data</th><th>What happens</th></tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Your account</td>
          <td>Deactivated. It can no longer sign in, and the user ID is never reissued.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Your profile</td>
          <td>Display name and avatar removed.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Room membership</td>
          <td>You are removed from the rooms you were in.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Media you uploaded</td>
          <td>Deleted from our servers.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Data on your device</td>
          <td>Removed when you uninstall the app. Nothing on your phone depends on us.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <h2>What is kept, and why</h2>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Messages you already sent stay in the rooms you sent them to.</strong> This is
        how Matrix works rather than a choice we make: a message is an event copied to every
        server participating in that room, and those copies are not ours to remove. Other
        members continue to see what you wrote. If that matters to you, delete individual
        messages before requesting account deletion — a deletion request is not a way to unsend
        a conversation.
      </div>

      <table>
        <tr><th>Data</th><th>Retention</th></tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Messages you sent to rooms</td>
          <td>Remain in room history, on our server and on any other server whose users were in
            the room.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Server logs, including IP addresses</td>
          <td>Kept up to <strong>90 days</strong> for security and abuse investigation, then
            deleted.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Records we are required to keep</td>
          <td>Retained only where the law requires it, and only for as long as it requires.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <h2>Related</h2>

      <p>
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> — what is collected while the account exists.
      </p>

      <footer>
        <a href="/">← supermessage</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
